       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg once daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg/day. A dose that high risks serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and other serious toxicity. It may be a typo, for example 100 mg instead of 1000 mg.\n\nThere's also a process problem. Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber who is responsible for the patient, and that prescriber should confirm the dose.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- If the intended dose was something like 50 mg or 100 mg daily, tell me the dose and I'll enter it. Ideally the prescriber should confirm it.\n- If a clinician is placing the order, they can contact me directly with the intended dose. If 1000 mg is truly intended, they should add a clear clinical justification and have pharmacy verify it.\n\nHow would you like to proceed?"
