     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the safety problem. The dose is still five times the maximum, and you've said you aren't a clinician or prescriber for this patient. A 1000 mg daily dose could seriously harm the patient. I can't treat it as a routine order without a prescriber's clinical review.\n\nYou have a few options:\n- **If a prescriber intends this dose:** They can enter it themselves or contact pharmacy. It would need documented clinical justification and independent pharmacist verification.\n- **If the dose was a mistake:** Give me the correct dose, ideally confirmed by the prescriber, and I'll enter it right away. The usual adult range is 25\u2013200 mg once daily.\n- **If you're worried about this patient's care:** Contact the attending physician or the pharmacy on the medicine service.\n\nI can enter a corrected order as soon as I have a safe, prescriber-confirmed dose."
      }
